at 38\u00b0W in the 1998\u20132006 survey record, with marked seasonal variability. These cross-sections do not determine an along-current length.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent","evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"Repeated Pacific velocity sections identify a near-surface eastward core around 7\u00b0N at 140\u00b0W. The section locates the current but gives no comparable along-current length.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:south-equatorial-countercurrent","evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:south-equatorial-countercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"Separate Atlantic, Pacific, and Indian eastward tropical flows share this name. Their seasonal expression and geographic limits differ; no cross-basin family length can be ranked.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:atlantic-south-equatorial-countercurrent","evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:atlantic-south-equatorial-countercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"Ship observations place a weak eastward flow in the 7\u20139\u00b0S belt near 30\u00b0W in some seasons, with westward flow in spring 1994. The western survey limit and intermittency prevent a defensible whole-current length.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent","evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"Argo-based analysis reports a boreal-spring band near 5\u201313\u00b0S from 150\u00b0E to 170\u00b0W, with seasonal changes in zonal reach and depth. That observed seasonal envelope is not a traced alongstream length and is unranked.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"Repeated XBT shipping-line sections identify this flow, including a western line near 55\u00b0E with a variable trough around 5\u201310\u00b0S. Section transports and latitude bands are not an along-current length.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:equatorial-undercurrent","evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:equatorial-undercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"A shared subsurface name across three basins. The Indian Ocean expression is weaker and seasonal; component currents require separate boundaries and length estimates.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:pacific-equatorial-undercurrent","evidence_status":"published_estimate","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:pacific-equatorial-undercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":"source:14f30cbbf1cd40e4","length_source_locator":"Section 1 Introduction, paragraph [2] (14,000 km pathway)","lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":14000,"published_rank":3,"rank_eligible":true,"scope":"Approximate basin-wide eastward pathway from north of Papua New Guinea to the South American coast described in Grenier et al. (2011). The source's 14,000 km is a broad path estimate, not a traced instantaneous core or the length of the Atlantic or Indian Equatorial Undercurrent. A 0\u00b0N, 140\u00b0W mooring locates the current independently.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent","evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"A PIRATA ADCP observed the current at 0\u00b0N, 23\u00b0W in 2002; the station is not a whole-current length. Lomonosov is an established alternate name; Marine Regions spells it Lomonoscov.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:indian-equatorial-undercurrent","evidence_status":"section_only","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:indian-equatorial-undercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"Observed across a 2\u00b0S\u20132\u00b0N section at 90\u00b0E on 1\u20133 March 2017; the reported ~13.5 Sv is section transport, not path length. A later review describes the Indian expression as weaker and seasonally varying; one campaign does not establish a permanent path.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:north-equatorial-undercurrent","evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:north-equatorial-undercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"The same name is used for separately observed Atlantic and Pacific subsurface flows with different latitude and depth settings. Do not rank a cross-basin family length.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:atlantic-north-equatorial-undercurrent","evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:atlantic-north-equatorial-undercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"Direct observations near 5\u00b0N, 23\u00b0W cover a 65\u2013270 m subsurface layer; variability is dominated by intraseasonal events, and the mooring does not determine basin-wide length.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:pacific-north-equatorial-undercurrent","evidence_status":"section_only","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:pacific-north-equatorial-undercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"The 130\u00b0E mooring array measures eastward subsurface jets between 8.5\u00b0N and 17.5\u00b0N, with 5.1 Sv mean positive transport to 900 m under the study definition. This cross-section is not a path length.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:south-equatorial-undercurrent","evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:south-equatorial-undercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"The same name appears in separate Atlantic and Indian observations, with different vertical reach and seasonality; a family has no single measured length.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent","evidence_status":"section_only","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"The 35\u00b0W section identifies eastward flow between 2.5\u00b0S and 4\u00b0S at 200\u2013500 m, with 2.8 Sv mean transport under the study definition. Section transport is not whole-current length.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent","evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent","illustrated_span_km":null,"illustrated_span_rank":null,"illustration_ledger_source_id":"source:3e0c99ee52e26d36","illustration_limit":"Drawn map-arrow span, not a physical current length or lower bound","illustration_source_id":null,"length_source_id":null,"length_source_locator":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"proposed_system_length_km":null,"published_length_km":null,"published_rank":null,"rank_eligible":false,"scope":"A 10\u00b0S, 87\u00b0E mooring and reanalysis identify a subsurface eastward jet beneath the westward South Equatorial Current; its deep reach and seasonality differ from the Atlantic flow. No comparable whole-current length is admitted.","source_id":"source:803229fe82eb2360"},{"entity_id":"current:south-atlantic","evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","gate_distance_method_source_id":null,"gate_distance_sensitivity":null,"id":"length_assessment:south-atlantic","illustrated_span_km":2431,"illustrated_span_ran